# Every path needs a maintainer review. Two of these matter more than the rest.
#
# .claude/ holds a hook script. A hook is executable content that a contributor's tooling may run
# locally, so a change to it deserves the same scrutiny as a change to a build target, and more
# than a change to source. It is deliberately not wired up by committed configuration, which is
# the primary control; this is the second one.
#
# .github/workflows/ holds the gates that check the two claims the project is sold on. A change
# that weakens one is worth noticing.

*                       @arnelirobles
/.claude/               @arnelirobles
/.github/               @arnelirobles
/src/Mapsicle/          @arnelirobles
/Directory.Packages.props  @arnelirobles
